lesson: 232
title: Teams of rugby and other football
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: A rugby union team has 15 players on the pitch, and so does a Gaelic football team and a hurling team (rugby league has 13, Australian rules 18).
explain: A match is two teams, so a 15-a-side match has 2 × 15 = 30 players on the pitch.
explain: 3 rugby union matches played at the same time: 3 × 30 = 90 players on the pitches.
vars: a=name n=2..6
answer: n * 30
exercise: On Saturday, rugby union matches are played on {n} pitches at the same time. How many players are on the pitches?
exercise: A club holds {n} Gaelic football matches at once on its pitches. How many players are on the pitches, not counting substitutes?
exercise: {n} hurling matches are going on at the same time at a festival. How many players are on the pitches?
exercise: {a} watches {n} rugby union matches at a tournament, one after another. How many players does {a.he} see start the matches?
exercise: How many players start {n} rugby union matches?
exercise: A county ground has {n} hurling pitches, and a match is being played on every one. How many players are on the grass?
exercise: {n} rugby matches on at the club, union not league. how many players on the pitches
exercise: gaelic matches on {n} pitches this arvo, no subs. how many players out there
exercise: hurling, {n+1} matches, no wait {n}. how many players on the pitch altogether
exercise: {n} rugby union games at once, plus the refs but don't count them. how many players
exercise: my cousin says a rugby union match has 26 players on the pitch?? anyway {n} matches going at once, how many players really
test: How many players run onto the pitches when {n} Gaelic football matches kick off together?
test: Every player in {n} rugby union matches needs a gum shield. How many gum shields are needed?
test: {n} hurling matches throw in at the same moment. Count the players on the field.
test: At kick-off, how many players stand on the pitches if rugby union is played on {n} of them?
test: union rugby, {n} games, how many players on at kick off
test: {n} hurling games n each player got a hurl, how many hurls (no subs)
test: A rugby league match is on next door but is not counted; {n} rugby union matches are played here. How many players are on the pitches here?
exam: Determine the aggregate number of players present upon the field of play when {n.words} matches of rugby union are contested simultaneously.
exam: It is given that {n} Gaelic football fixtures commence concurrently. Ascertain the total number of players thereby deployed, substitutes being excluded.
exam: Compute the total complement of players participating at the commencement of {n} hurling matches.
exam: Whereas {n} matches under the laws of rugby union are in progress, state the number of players on the field of play.
exercise: {n+1} rugby union matches were planned, but one pitch was "not fit for play" after the storm and that match was off. The other matches are played at the same time. How many players are on the pitches?
exercise: one match "postponed due to unforeseen circumstances", both teams got the runs lol. was {n+1} rugby union matches, rest go ahead. how many players on the pitches
test: The coach was economical with the truth: he said there were {n*30+15} players on the pitches. In fact {n} Gaelic football matches were being played. How many players were really on the pitches?
